<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak Dec real ind output up 1.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Slovak Dec real ind output up 1.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovak real industrial output rose 1.4 percent, year-on-year, in December, putting output up 2.5 percent for the whole of 1996, the Slovak Statistical Bureau (SUSR) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It added that overall 1996 Slovak industrial production totalled 531.8 billion crowns, compared to a real increase of 8.3 percent and a total of 497.239 billion crowns for 1995.  </p>
<p> SLOVAK INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  Dec 96   Nov 96   Dec 95  FY 96</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr	   +1.4	0.0	+8.3   +2.5</p>
<p>Construction Output</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr	   +3.2     +6.4	-1.6   +3.7</p>
<p>Note. All figures are subject to revision.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-521-8402</p>
